        {
          "no": 14,
          "code": "00010944",
          "description": "Maldives Beach Safety",
          "note": "The Maldives are famous for their beautiful seas, but do exercise care whilst on \nholiday in the Maldives. Due to the nature of the properties in the Maldives many \nrooms and common areas have direct access to the beach/water and many \nwalkways do not have handrails or balustrades. \nPlease check out the beach when you arrive and look out for safety information \ne.g. warning flags and safety signs and adhere to them at all times. Never swim \nalone, make sure there are always other people around. If travelling with children\nmake sure they are supervised by an adult at all times. Be aware of dangerous rip \ncurrents and strong tides and look out for large waves when entering and exiting \nthe water.",
          "dateModified": "2023-06-29T15:07:54",
          "external": true,
          "internal": true,
